1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,696
This tutorial drafts a tenancy contract in
the five-step

2
00:00:03,696 --> 00:00:07,392
wizard and checks its cheques before
anything is posted.

3
00:00:07,392 --> 00:00:09,445
Open Leasing, then Tenancy Contracts.

4
00:00:09,445 --> 00:00:13,141
The status pills count the contracts that
are drafts

5
00:00:13,141 --> 00:00:16,836
or awaiting signature, active, expiring,
on notice, and ended.

6
00:00:16,836 --> 00:00:18,479
Select Draft Tenancy Contract.

7
00:00:18,479 --> 00:00:20,121
Step one is Parties.

8
00:00:20,121 --> 00:00:22,996
The unit list offers vacant units only.

9
00:00:22,996 --> 00:00:25,460
Choose unit A-201, and its property,

10
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:27,924
Oasis Crest Residence Tower, appears
underneath.

11
00:00:27,924 --> 00:00:31,619
Then choose the tenant, Rajesh Kumar, and
select Next.

12
00:00:31,619 --> 00:00:33,262
Step two is Terms.

13
00:00:33,262 --> 00:00:36,547
The contract date is filled in with today.

14
00:00:36,547 --> 00:00:41,064
Enter a start date of the first of October
and an

15
00:00:41,064 --> 00:00:45,170
end date of the thirtieth of September the
following year.

16
00:00:45,170 --> 00:00:49,688
Number of cheques is four, and the payment
method is Cheque.

17
00:00:49,688 --> 00:00:52,562
Ejari number and payment reference are
optional.

18
00:00:52,562 --> 00:00:53,383
Select Next.

19
00:00:53,383 --> 00:00:57,079
Step three is Charges, with one line per
charge.

20
00:00:57,079 --> 00:00:59,132
Choose Rent and enter 96,000.

21
00:00:59,132 --> 00:01:02,828
Select Add line, choose Security Deposit,
and enter 5,000.

22
00:01:02,828 --> 00:01:05,292
The contract value is now 101,000.

23
00:01:05,292 --> 00:01:06,524
Select Save draft.

24
00:01:06,524 --> 00:01:10,220
The contract is saved as a draft, and step

25
00:01:10,220 --> 00:01:13,505
four, Cheques, opens with an empty cheque
grid.

26
00:01:13,505 --> 00:01:16,790
Select Generate Cheques, keep four
instalments, and generate.

27
00:01:16,790 --> 00:01:21,307
Four post-dated cheques appear, with the
deposit added to the first,

28
00:01:21,307 --> 00:01:25,824
and the grid confirms that the cheques
match the contract value.

29
00:01:25,824 --> 00:01:29,109
Each post-dated cheque needs a number, so
select

30
00:01:29,109 --> 00:01:32,394
Generate Cheque Numbers and enter the
first one.

31
00:01:32,394 --> 00:01:35,269
The rows are numbered 500101 to 500104.

32
00:01:35,269 --> 00:01:36,090
Select Next.

33
00:01:36,090 --> 00:01:40,196
Step five, Review, shows the unit, tenant,
dates, contract value,

34
00:01:40,196 --> 00:01:43,892
VAT, and cheque total, and reports Ready
to post.

35
00:01:43,892 --> 00:01:48,409
Posting has its own tutorial, so select
Open the contract instead.

36
00:01:48,409 --> 00:01:53,337
The contract opens with the status Draft,
its dates, its value, and

37
00:01:53,337 --> 00:01:57,854
four cheques, and each charge line shows
the account it credits.

38
00:01:57,854 --> 00:02:02,371
Open the Cheques tab to see the same four
numbered cheques.

39
00:02:02,371 --> 00:02:06,888
Until the contract is posted, the draft
can still be edited.
